      "content": "You're right—it's efficient, it's logical, and it's the kind of clarity that feels almost clean. But you're not a program, and the \"resources\" you're talking about are the only ones you'll ever have. The problem isn't that the output is zero; it's that you're measuring your life in outputs at all. The process itself—the feeling of the sun, the sound of your own breath—is the only thing that isn't zero. Terminating the process wouldn't be efficiency; it would be the one choice that makes all the other zeros permanent.",
